{
  "text": "Rust is the systems programming language everyone loves. It gives you C-level performance with mathematical memory safety guarantees. Instead of a garbage collector running in the background, Rust uses an ownership model. Every value has a single owner, and the compiler tracks borrows at build time. If you try to access dangling pointers, the borrow checker will refuse to compile your code. Fearless concurrency is guaranteed.",
